  "chapter_note": "This chapter is a biographical/hagiographical narrative about Mani's missionary journeys to King Sapores, to Persia, Babylon, the Medes and Parthians. There is essentially NO cosmological-correspondential substrate here — no five-fold mappings, no zoomorphic correspondences, no realm-onto-realm structures. The entire chapter is autobiographical apostolic frame: Mani's first-person travel narrative (\"I am a single Anointed... I came to the world... I went to the land of Persia\"), interactions with Sapores, his disciple Aurades, the rejection by archons/kings/satraps/governors. Embedded polemical vocabulary (ⲇⲟⲅⲙⲁ at i=122) shows the editor's contemporary religious controversies. Closes with hortatory exhortation to pray and stand firm, then the disciple's praise speech. The whole chapter is the editorial layer in narrative mode — the genre is missionary hagiography, not cosmic teaching. Editorial fatigue score (+0.44) confirms apostolic_dialogue vocabulary intensifies in second half. Heavy manuscript damage (92.9%).",
